# Initiative docs need a TLDR

When creating a new markdown file under `Initiatives/`, put a **TLDR** section immediately after the title and any one-line subtitle.

- 3–6 short sentences. The conclusion, not a table of contents.
- Plain language. No unexplained shorthand.
- A reader who only reads the TLDR should know the decision and why it matters.

```markdown
# How we show (and do not show) causation

Working model for skills → deals → revenue.

## TLDR

We can put deal value next to skill scores. That shows they go together, not that skill caused the money.
```

Do not skip the TLDR on READMEs, discovery notes, PRDs, or process docs created from now on. Do not retrofit old files unless asked.
